1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,183
Throw a ball straight up.

2
00:00:02,183 --> 00:00:06,440
It passes fifteen metres twice,
once going up and once coming down.

3
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:10,089
It reaches twenty metres
only once, right at the top.

4
00:00:10,089 --> 00:00:11,569
And twenty five metres?

5
00:00:11,569 --> 00:00:12,469
Never.

6
00:00:12,569 --> 00:00:15,154
Aarav tried this on his way home today.

7
00:00:15,504 --> 00:00:18,102
Every height gives the
same kind of equation.

8
00:00:18,102 --> 00:00:20,657
So why two answers, then one, then none?

9
00:00:21,157 --> 00:00:23,519
The twist: even never has two answers.

10
00:00:23,519 --> 00:00:25,660
They just live off the number line.

11
00:00:26,310 --> 00:00:29,191
Each height question is
a quadratic equation.

12
00:00:29,541 --> 00:00:31,978
A quadratic equation looks like this.

13
00:00:31,978 --> 00:00:36,426
a x squared, plus b x, plus c,
equals zero, with a not zero.

14
00:00:36,826 --> 00:00:39,984
a, b and c are fixed
numbers, the coefficients.

15
00:00:39,984 --> 00:00:42,916
The x values that make
it true are the roots.

16
00:00:43,316 --> 00:00:48,419
For the ball at fifteen metres, twenty
t minus five t squared equals fifteen.

17
00:00:48,819 --> 00:00:54,246
Tidy up and divide by five: t squared
minus four t plus three equals zero.

18
00:00:54,646 --> 00:00:58,110
It factors into t minus
one, times t minus three.

19
00:00:58,110 --> 00:01:01,350
One second going up,
three seconds coming down.

20
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:03,540
Now the whole family.

21
00:01:03,540 --> 00:01:06,280
y equals x squared minus four x plus c.

22
00:01:06,280 --> 00:01:09,170
For the ball, c is the height over five.

23
00:01:09,570 --> 00:01:12,560
The roots are where the
curve meets the x axis.

24
00:01:12,560 --> 00:01:13,719
Let c count up.

25
00:01:14,119 --> 00:01:17,374
At c equals zero, the
roots are zero and four.

26
00:01:17,374 --> 00:01:19,999
As c grows, the roots slide together.

27
00:01:20,399 --> 00:01:22,842
At c equals four, they meet at two.

28
00:01:22,842 --> 00:01:24,935
The curve just touches the axis.

29
00:01:24,935 --> 00:01:26,592
The two roots are equal.

30
00:01:26,992 --> 00:01:29,407
Past four, the curve leaves the axis.

31
00:01:29,407 --> 00:01:30,882
No real root is left.

32
00:01:30,882 --> 00:01:33,076
But look at the map on the right.

33
00:01:33,476 --> 00:01:37,302
The roots have stepped off the
number line, one up, one down.

34
00:01:37,302 --> 00:01:40,774
At c equals five, they are
two plus i and two minus i.

35
00:01:41,424 --> 00:01:42,343
Quick one.

36
00:01:42,343 --> 00:01:45,827
At c equals six, are the
roots real or complex?

37
00:01:45,827 --> 00:01:47,126
Pause and think.

38
00:01:50,326 --> 00:01:51,226
Complex!

39
00:01:51,059 --> 00:01:53,932
Past four the curve stays above the axis.

40
00:01:53,932 --> 00:01:57,082
The roots are two plus
and minus i root two.

41
00:01:57,732 --> 00:01:59,828
Where do those roots come from?

42
00:01:59,828 --> 00:02:02,262
One formula works for every quadratic.

43
00:02:02,662 --> 00:02:03,562
Step one.

44
00:02:03,546 --> 00:02:07,199
Divide everything by a,
so x squared stands alone.

45
00:02:07,949 --> 00:02:08,849
Step two.

46
00:02:08,766 --> 00:02:11,088
Move c over a to the right side.

47
00:02:11,838 --> 00:02:12,738
Step three.

48
00:02:12,719 --> 00:02:15,628
Add b over two a, squared, to both sides.

49
00:02:15,628 --> 00:02:18,144
Now the left side is a perfect square.

50
00:02:18,894 --> 00:02:19,794
Step four.

51
00:02:19,754 --> 00:02:22,145
Take the square root of both sides.

52
00:02:22,145 --> 00:02:25,800
Plus or minus, because both
signs give the same square.

53
00:02:26,550 --> 00:02:27,544
Step five.

54
00:02:27,544 --> 00:02:29,429
Subtract b over two a.

55
00:02:29,429 --> 00:02:31,770
This is the quadratic formula.

56
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:36,077
On the curve, minus b over
two a is the middle line.

57
00:02:36,077 --> 00:02:39,169
The roots sit at equal
distances on either side.

58
00:02:39,569 --> 00:02:44,350
If b squared minus four a c is
negative, its square root is not real.

59
00:02:44,350 --> 00:02:49,030
But root minus one is i, so the
root becomes i times a real number.

60
00:02:49,030 --> 00:02:50,749
The formula still works.

61
00:02:51,399 --> 00:02:52,466
Side by side.

62
00:02:52,466 --> 00:02:56,180
x squared minus four x plus
three crosses the axis twice.

63
00:02:56,180 --> 00:02:58,925
The roots are one and three, both real.

64
00:02:59,325 --> 00:03:01,692
x squared minus four x plus five.

65
00:03:01,692 --> 00:03:03,998
The curve never touches the axis.

66
00:03:03,998 --> 00:03:08,752
Under the root is minus four, so the
roots are two plus i and two minus

67
00:03:08,752 --> 00:03:09,652
i.

68
00:03:09,770 --> 00:03:14,095
Same real part, opposite
imaginary parts: a conjugate pair.

69
00:03:14,095 --> 00:03:18,649
With real coefficients, complex
roots always come in such pairs.

70
00:03:19,049 --> 00:03:20,018
Your turn.

71
00:03:20,018 --> 00:03:23,859
Does x squared plus nine
equal zero have real roots?

72
00:03:23,859 --> 00:03:25,284
Pause and decide.

73
00:03:28,484 --> 00:03:29,384
No!

74
00:03:28,957 --> 00:03:33,253
x squared would be minus nine,
and no real square is negative.

75
00:03:33,253 --> 00:03:36,127
The roots are three i and minus three i.

76
00:03:36,777 --> 00:03:37,945
Remember this.

77
00:03:37,945 --> 00:03:40,739
Every quadratic equation has two roots.

78
00:03:40,739 --> 00:03:44,101
Real or complex, one
formula finds them both.

79
00:03:44,801 --> 00:03:46,537
Now, one worked example.

80
00:03:46,887 --> 00:03:50,231
Solve x squared plus x
plus one equals zero.

81
00:03:50,731 --> 00:03:51,631
Step one.

82
00:03:51,514 --> 00:03:53,642
Here a, b and c are all one.

83
00:03:54,392 --> 00:03:55,292
Step two.

84
00:03:55,208 --> 00:03:59,629
b squared minus four a c is one
minus four, which is minus three.

85
00:04:00,379 --> 00:04:01,293
Step three.

86
00:04:01,293 --> 00:04:04,469
The square root of minus
three is i root three.

87
00:04:05,219 --> 00:04:06,142
Step four.

88
00:04:06,142 --> 00:04:10,696
So x is minus one, plus or minus
i root three, all over two.

89
00:04:11,446 --> 00:04:15,520
A conjugate pair, both with
real part minus one half.

90
00:04:16,170 --> 00:04:17,636
Now, the exam trap.

91
00:04:17,986 --> 00:04:21,422
Solve x squared minus two
x plus five equals zero.

92
00:04:21,422 --> 00:04:23,688
Under the root is minus sixteen.

93
00:04:23,688 --> 00:04:27,801
Many students write minus four,
and get three and minus one.

94
00:04:28,201 --> 00:04:31,228
But the square root of
minus sixteen is four i.

95
00:04:31,228 --> 00:04:33,365
Check: three does not even fit.

96
00:04:33,365 --> 00:04:36,741
The roots are one plus two
i, and one minus two i.

97
00:04:37,391 --> 00:04:38,842
Where is this asked?

98
00:04:38,842 --> 00:04:43,351
In JEE Main, as in April twenty
nineteen: solve a quadratic with complex

99
00:04:43,351 --> 00:04:44,948
roots, then use them.

100
00:04:44,948 --> 00:04:47,412
It is not in the current NCERT text.

101
00:04:48,012 --> 00:04:49,254
Exam level now.

102
00:04:49,254 --> 00:04:53,863
These two roots and the origin make
a triangle on the Argand plane.

103
00:04:53,863 --> 00:04:55,052
Find its area.

104
00:04:55,052 --> 00:04:56,346
Pause and solve.

105
00:05:01,746 --> 00:05:02,955
The answer is B.

106
00:05:02,955 --> 00:05:03,855
Six.

107
00:05:03,932 --> 00:05:09,300
b squared minus four a c is sixteen
minus fifty two, which is minus thirty

108
00:05:09,300 --> 00:05:10,200
six.

109
00:05:10,377 --> 00:05:12,377
Its square root is six i.

110
00:05:12,377 --> 00:05:17,947
So x is four plus or minus six i, over
two: two plus three i, and two minus

111
00:05:17,947 --> 00:05:18,847
three i.

112
00:05:19,275 --> 00:05:22,727
The roots sit three above and
three below the point two.

113
00:05:22,727 --> 00:05:24,254
Base six, height two.

114
00:05:24,254 --> 00:05:26,227
Half of six times two is six.

115
00:05:26,827 --> 00:05:28,288
Here is your recap.

116
00:05:28,288 --> 00:05:29,789
Screenshot this card.

117
00:05:32,989 --> 00:05:35,825
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

118
00:05:36,226 --> 00:05:37,126
One.

119
00:05:36,786 --> 00:05:39,608
Solve x squared plus four equals zero.

120
00:05:40,507 --> 00:05:41,407
Two.

121
00:05:41,053 --> 00:05:43,975
Why does the formula need plus or minus?

122
00:05:44,875 --> 00:05:45,775
Three.

123
00:05:45,518 --> 00:05:50,081
Three minus two i is a root of a
quadratic with real coefficients.

124
00:05:50,081 --> 00:05:51,872
What is the other root?

125
00:05:52,972 --> 00:05:58,078
Next time: one small number tells you
if the roots are real, equal or complex,

126
00:05:58,078 --> 00:05:59,348
before you solve.

127
00:05:59,348 --> 00:06:00,557
The discriminant.
